Q-SF 001-SF-001 — Customer Intelligence Engine. Your first trigger.

Story: As a Customer Success manager, I want customer tiers assigned automatically from annual revenue, so my team stops doing it by hand.

Rules:

AnnualRevenue	Tier
≥ 10,000,000 (1 crore)	Platinum
≥ 5,000,000 (50 lakhs)	Gold
≥ 1,000,000 (10 lakhs)	Silver
below that	Bronze

Setup (admin work — 2 min, your home turf): create a custom field on Account — Customer_Tier__c, type Text(20) or a picklist with those four values.

Acceptance criteria:

Tier is set when an Account is created
Tier is recalculated when AnnualRevenue changes
Works for a single record saved in the UI
Works for 200 records inserted at once (test this: build a List of 200 Accounts with varying revenues in Anonymous Apex, insert, then query and spot-check the tiers)
AnnualRevenue is null → decide the rule and comment it (Bronze? leave tier blank? your call — but decide)
Zero SOQL queries and zero DML statements inside the trigger

ANS
trigger AccountTrigger on Account (before insert,before update) {
    for(Account acc: Trigger.new){
        if(acc.AnnualRevenue==null){
            acc.Customer_Tier__c='';
        }else if(acc.AnnualRevenue>=10000000){
            acc.Customer_Tier__c='Platinum';
        }else if(acc.AnnualRevenue>=5000000 ){
            acc.Customer_Tier__c='Gold';
        }else if(acc.AnnualRevenue>=1000000){
            acc.Customer_Tier__c='Silver';
        }else if(acc.AnnualRevenue<1000000 && acc.AnnualRevenue>0){
            acc.Customer_Tier__c='Bronze';
        }
    }

}

